ew" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA KENWOOD</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA, SHOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORII AKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA SHOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORII, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA, SHOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRAISHI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A BS digital broadcasting receiver which eliminates the uncertainty of an ODU's phase noise-dependent switching point when switching a receiving system.  The receiver is provided with a demodulator circuit (6A) having a carrier regenerating circuit (19A) based on demodulation data in a BPSK modulation section, and with a demodulator circuit (6B) having a carrier regenerating circuit (19B) based on demodulation data in each time-division modulation section, wherein, when a lock for carriers regenerated by the carrier regenerating circuit (19A) is maintained and carriers regenerated by the carrier regenerating circuit (19B) is locked, demodulation data, in the BPSK demodulation section and a QPSK demodulation section, output from the demodulator circuit (6A) and 8-PSK-modulated demodulation data output from the demodulator circuit (6B) are selected by a selector (7) for outputting.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un récepteur pour station de base radio numérique éliminant les incertitudes du point de commutation de phase ODU dépendant du bruit lors de la commutation du système de réception. Le récepteur est muni d'un circuit de démodulation (6A) à circuit de régénération des porteuses (19A) utilisant les données de démodulation d'une section de modulation MDPB et un circuit de démodulation (6B) à circuit de régénération des porteuses (19B) utilisant les données de démodulation de chacune des sections de modulation à division temporelle. Lorsqu'on maintient le verrouillage des porteuses régénérées par le circuit de régénération des porteuses (19B) les données de démodulation des sections de modulation MDBF et MDPQ émises par le circuit de démodulation (6A), et les données de démodulation modulées en MDP-8 émises par le circuit de démodulation (6B) sont sélectionnées par un sélecteur (7) en vue de leur émission.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>